-- title:
--   Irreducibility of the modular polynomial over K(jqNModC_M)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, let $M$ be a nonzero natural number, and let `data` be a `ModularPolynomialData M`: a polynomial $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ that is monic (as a polynomial in $Y$), whose $Y$-degree equals $\psi(M) = \sum_{d \mid M,\ d \text{ squarefree}} M/d$ (the Dedekind $\psi$-function, `dedekindPsi`), and which satisfies $\Phi(\mathrm{jq},\, \mathrm{jqN}\,M) = 0$ in the Laurent series field over $\mathbb{Q}$, the substitution in the coefficients being $X \mapsto \mathrm{jq}$. Assume that $M$ is nonzero in $K$, i.e. $(M : K) \neq 0$. Inside `LaurentSeries K` form the intermediate field $K(\mathrm{jqNModC}\,K\,M)$ generated over $K$ by the distinguished series `jqNModC K M`, and let `toJqNField` be the one-variable polynomial over this field obtained from $\Phi$ by mapping each coefficient polynomial in $\mathbb{Z}[X]$ through $X \mapsto \mathrm{jqNModC}\,K\,M$ (the generator `jqNGen`). The conclusion is that this polynomial is irreducible in $K(\mathrm{jqNModC}\,K\,M)[Y]$. Thus irreducibility is asserted for $\Phi(\mathrm{jqNModC}\,K\,M,\,Y)$ over the field generated by the level-$M$ series, the classical statement transported by $q \mapsto q^M$.
--
--   This is the classical irreducibility of the modular equation $\Phi_M(j, Y)$ over the rational function field in $j$, in the form valid over any field in which $M$ is invertible, and equivalently the assertion that $\Phi_M(j,Y)$ is the minimal polynomial of the level-$M$ $j$-series. It is used in the construction of the automorphisms of the modular function field, as in [`ModularCurve.exists_algEquiv_modularFunctionFieldC_apply_jGeomGen_eq_comp`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_algEquiv_modularFunctionFieldC_apply_jGeomGen_eq_comp) and [`ModularCurve.exists_algEquiv_modularFunctionFieldC_swap_and_charLDegeneracyRoof_swap`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_algEquiv_modularFunctionFieldC_swap_and_charLDegeneracyRoof_swap).
